  "details": "Description\n\n3.5mm microphone input seems to be peaking audio even at 5% sensitivity with nosie supression on, please fix this when you can <3\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nPersonally I am using earphones (specifically a pair of Sony MDR-EX155) connected via the front 3.5mm input on my pc case (Thermaltake Versa h21), running Zorin OS core 18.1, the input driver is labeled as \"Family 17H/19H HD Audio Driver\" ... I hope this info helps.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Audio\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.4.1p1-1937-299983b13b-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report",
